BND-03: let an outfall's CONCEN inflow set the quality of its reverse flow

The input reference allows a CONCEN inflow without a FLOW inflow at an
outfall, so that a pollutant enters with reverse flow. InflowSolver::
computeAll() multiplied the concentration by the outfall's FLOW inflow
only, so without one the CONCEN inflow did nothing. Make the outfall hold
the CONCEN value as its quality (conc_old, already rolled for this step): a
supplying outfall receives no flow, so mixAtNodes() keeps the held value and
the reverse flow carries it into the network. Same change as the 5.3.0
patch.

The reverse flow's mass is booked by BND-04, not here.

Requires: BND-04

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-03_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Inflow.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Inflow.cpp
